// A malformed word names nothing at every generation: releasing it faults the
// process with "bad handle".
//
//   SOS malformed: releasing a word whose index field is zero
//   SOS: process fault: bad handle process=0
//   SOS: process teardown handles=3 ... process=0
//
// The regression this catches: with an unsplit word, "names nothing" was
// `word == NO_HANDLE` and that test was complete. With a split word it is not:
// `0x100` is a generation of 1 over an index field of zero, it is not equal to
// `NO_HANDLE`, and a lookup that kept the whole-word test would take it as a
// real handle and index the table with it. The kernel's rule is that the index
// field carries a 1-based index, so zero is not an index at any generation, and
// `lookup_handle` tests the field.
//
// The probe is valid at every split, which matters because `HANDLE_INDEX_BITS`
// is configurable. At the default eight bits this word is index 0 at generation
// 1, refused because zero is not an index. At a wider index field it is index
// 256, refused because the table has nothing like that many entries. Either way
// it names nothing, and a kernel that let it through would be reading out of
// bounds or handing out slot 0, so the case keeps checking the thing it was
// written for without knowing where the boundary sits.
//
// It is spelled at the C altitude because the typed layer has no way to build a
// handle from a word, so the mistake only exists one floor down.
//
// One fault per case: a fault ends the process.

import sos.{System, sos_handle_release}

static EXIT_FAILED: UInt = 1

/// A word a hostile or buggy process might write: generation bits set over an
/// index field of zero.
///
/// A deliberate magic number. It is not derived from `HANDLE_INDEX_BITS`
/// because it is untrusted input, a number chosen by the process and not by the
/// encoding, and the claim is that the kernel refuses it whatever the encoding
/// happens to be. See the header for why it is refused at every split.
static MALFORMED: UInt = 0x100

@export("_start")
func _start(boot_handle: UInt) {
    let system = System(boot_handle: boot_handle)

    let _ = system.debug_print("SOS malformed: releasing a word whose index field is zero\n")

    // Does not return.
    let _ = sos_handle_release(MALFORMED)

    let _ = system.debug_print("SOS malformed: survived, which is the bug\n")
    let _ = system.shutdown(EXIT_FAILED)
}
